# DevUniverse

This project has the devuniverse skill at `skills/devuniverse/SKILL.md`
in this repo (or wherever you copied the `skills/devuniverse/` folder).
Read that file in full before using it.

Quick reference:
- First use: `bash skills/devuniverse/scripts/bootstrap.sh` (clones/builds
  the real devuniverse-mcp server into a local cache — one-time, safe to
  re-run; builds clean from a fresh clone).
- Full tool catalog with exact JSON argument shapes:
  `skills/devuniverse/references/tools.md`.
- Call a tool: `bash skills/devuniverse/scripts/call.sh <tool_name> '<json-args>'`.
- `init_dev_universe` is the real starting point for a new project — one
  call runs the full agency debate, scaffold, Figma sync, compliance
  audit, and asset watcher.
- `provision_omnicinema` with `confirm:true` clones and runs code on the
  user's machine — confirm with the user first, the tool itself can't
  ask.
- `generate_compliance_docs` output is a structured draft, not legal
  advice — say so if you hand it to the user.
